Comparison of one month (Jan), focus on Ant., for 70 deg threshold (hoping to
see impacts of energy extraction in deep snowpack in Ant, like we were prev
seeing in S. Greenland),

Monthly map notes
-----------------
ELM monthly records are labeled using the midpoint of time_bounds. The time
coordinate itself is the interval endpoint (e.g. February 1 for January's
average), so using its month would shift every map by one month. This also
applies when a file contains only one record. Without bounds, an exact
month-start endpoint is assigned to the preceding month.

MPAS maps use native cell polygons from restart-file verticesOnCell,
nEdgesOnCell, latVertex, and lonVertex. Values are not interpolated between
cell centers. This avoids the artificial gaps produced by a global edge-length
cutoff on a longitude/latitude Delaunay triangulation, especially at high
latitudes. Light blue is the ocean background, not a runoff-flux value.

Run plot_maps.py in the E3SM unified environment to regenerate the configured
maps. Existing figures with the same output names are overwritten.
